<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simplifying factorial quotients and evaluating consecutive integer products</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> Simplify \(\displaystyle \frac{{@pm@}!}{{@pm_m2@}!}\) and give your answer as a whole number.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{{@pm@}!}{{@pm_m2@}!} =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>(b)</b> Evaluate the product \({@pm2@} \times {@pm2_m1@} \times {@pm2_m2@}\) as a single value, using factorial notation to help you organize the calculation.</p>
<p>\({@pm2@} \times {@pm2_m1@} \times {@pm2_m2@} =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a):</b><br>
Expand the larger factorial in the numerator only until it matches \({@pm_m2@}!\) in the denominator, then cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@pm@}!}{{@pm_m2@}!} = \frac{{@pm@} \times {@pm_m1@} \times {@pm_m2@}!}{{@pm_m2@}!} = {@pm@} \times {@pm_m1@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@pm@}!}{{@pm_m2@}!} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b):</b><br>
This product consists of the first \(3\) consecutive factors of \({@pm2@}!\), so in factorial notation it equals \(\displaystyle \frac{{@pm2@}!}{{@pm2_m3@}!}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@pm2@} \times {@pm2_m1@} \times {@pm2_m2@} = \frac{{@pm2@}!}{{@pm2_m3@}!} = {@pm2_step1@} \times {@pm2_m2@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {@pm2@} \times {@pm2_m1@} \times {@pm2_m2@} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
